microsoft.com Microsoft builds AI-powered platforms, tools, and services for consumers, businesses, and governments. Beginning in fiscal 2027 it reports two segments. Agents and Infra is the dominant segment. It includes:
- the Azure cloud and AI infrastructure platform;
- Microsoft 365 commercial and consumer cloud productivity subscriptions;
- productivity and server licensing;
- industry solutions;
- frontier and support services. Devices and Consumer includes:
- search and advertising;
- Xbox gaming content, services, and hardware;
- Windows OEM licensing and devices. The company's Microsoft Cloud offerings generate a large and growing share of revenue, backed by a substantial commercial remaining performance obligation. Microsoft is investing heavily in data center and AI infrastructure to meet demand for AI and agent workloads, and it holds an investment in OpenAI that materially affects reported GAAP earnings. Its stated mission is to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more, with a focus on making AI broadly available and responsible. Updated Oct 28, 2026 A decade in bonds returned 16%, less than half the 39% rise in US inflation, while NVIDIA compounded past 11,000%. Cramer is telling holders of AI infrastructure names that the washout is unfinished, and that a strong jobs report did nothing to help. The one place he is willing to put money is Cisco, which he thinks has been dragged down with everything else. Applied Materials gets the opposite treatment: its lower price still looks expensive because the old price was built on a squeeze. The day after IonQ filed its Q3 2026 results with the SEC, buyers pushed the quantum name 12.64% above its $28.01 open. Peers moved far less, with Microsoft up 1.52% and IBM up 1.09%. Retail traders are piling into the AI trade again, staying bullish on AMD, Super Micro and Microsoft, while Alphabet draws the biggest argument of the day at 346 comments. Trump Media is souring fast after the midterms, and Meta chatter is heating up. Cramer's read flips the AI trade on its head: regulation that curbs data center construction relieves memory costs for Apple and spending pressure for Microsoft and Amazon, while hitting the chipmakers that need the build to continue. He cautions the move is only a one-day trade, with Friday's payroll report capable of undoing much of it. Microsoft closed at $555.80, a fresh 52-week high that clears the October 13 peak by 2.27% and puts the $4.1 trillion software giant back in price discovery after a spring trough near $356. The leadership baton is being passed to second-tier data center names, and Cramer would rather own companies with clean balance sheets than the big caps issuing debt and equity to stay in the AI race. He is not calling a bottom yet: without a high-volume reversal day, he keeps money elsewhere. Intel tops the board on the fewest comments of the group, with 3,184 upvotes piled onto a bearish take. Big Tech names stay split ahead of earnings, Reddit's own stock is heating up, and Caterpillar chatter is souring. Four of the market's largest cash machines now spend $201.9 billion a quarter on AI buildout, so the free cash flow that funded buybacks and dividends is the line to watch next earnings season. Owning "Big Tech" as one block no longer works if only two of the group are still trending higher, with Alphabet breaking down as AI search competition pressure mounts. One company sits at the center of a spending web that ties together six megacaps, and Steve Eisman thinks its stumble would ripple far beyond tech. Before you trust your index fund,… The tech stocks your portfolio treats as growth bets also mail checks every quarter. One pays the least yet raises fastest, another has paid since 1916, and each carries a hidden risk… A buyout can feel like freedom until the math shows up. One 55-year-old engineer has a generous severance, a looming Social Security gap, and a choice at 62 that could quietly shape… Alphabet has slid nearly 19% in a month while institutions quietly shift toward quality. One investor keeps buying each dip, yet a negative cash flow figure and heavy share-sale capacity could still… Wall Street's fear gauge just posted one of its biggest jumps in decades, and investors are hunting for safe harbors. One tech giant has a backlog, margins, and a spending problem that… One Number: $1 Trillion in a Single Morning US stocks added $1 trillion in market value in the opening period of trading on November 9, 2026, as dip buyers moved back into… Mega-cap internet stocks are climbing after JPMorgan updated its Analyst Focus List, and the moves show money rotating within Big Tech. Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META | META Price Prediction) stock is at $637.77,… Apple just posted its best year ever, yet a memory chip squeeze is eating into margins and one analyst still won't blink. Can the iPhone maker's cash machine outrun a cost shock… If you spent your working years treating technology stocks as too volatile for a retirement account, the landscape has shifted. A small group of mature tech giants now act like cash-generating dividend… A record quarter should have sent this chip giant soaring. Instead, the stock sank for a week straight while Wall Street analysts kept piling in. What do they see in custom silicon… Wall Street has almost entirely agreed on Nvidia, yet institutional filers are quietly splitting and a CEO probe is rattling the board. The case against the stock rests on financing exposure, thinning… While Microsoft pours over $100 billion into data centers, Apple barely lifts a finger on AI spending, and one investor keeps buying anyway. But a rising cost inside every iPhone could still… Cisco was the best business in the world at its peak, and its company kept growing for decades. So why did some of its shareholders lose a generation? The answer could decide… A $1 Trillion Price Tag $1 trillion. That is what one prospective investor now believes Anthropic may be worth after the latest technology selloff. In October, investors were talking about a valuation… Microsoft is quietly switching off the AI servers it rented from Oracle, and Oracle insists its aging GPUs still command a premium. Which story holds up, and what does it mean for… Microsoft builds AI-powered platforms, tools, and services for consumers, businesses, and governments. Beginning in fiscal 2027 it reports two segments. 24/7 Wall St.'s 12-month price target for MSFT is $670.06, rated Buy. The Wall Street consensus target is $634.14.									MSFT price prediction → This post may contain links from our sponsors and affiliates, and Flywheel Publishing may receive compensation for actions taken through them.				© 2026 24/7 Wall St.
